      "endSeconds": 13.175,
      "index": 0,
      "sceneId": "title",
      "startSeconds": 0.25,
      "text": "Bottom line: Microsoft is a portfolio, not one system; first map the need to Windows, Microsoft 365, Azure or Copilot, then verify entitlements early."
    },
    {
      "endSeconds": 26.475,
      "index": 1,
      "sceneId": "windows-layer",
      "startSeconds": 13.725,
      "text": "Start with Windows when the decision is the PC experience: devices, desktop, apps and user productivity. It anchors the endpoint for users, not every cloud service."
    },
    {
      "endSeconds": 40.6,
      "index": 2,
      "sceneId": "work-layer",
      "startSeconds": 27.025,
      "text": "Use Microsoft 365 when the need is everyday work: Office apps, email, files, meetings, sharing and collaboration. It packages work services, not custom infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "endSeconds": 53.45,
      "index": 3,
      "sceneId": "azure-layer",
      "startSeconds": 41.15,
      "text": "Use Azure when applications need cloud services: compute, storage, data and AI categories. It is the builder layer for apps and managed resources for teams."
    },
    {
      "endSeconds": 67.225,
      "index": 4,
      "sceneId": "copilot-layer",
      "startSeconds": 54.0,
      "text": "Treat Copilot as AI assistance that sits inside selected workflows and licenses. Confirm access, grounding, service availability and subscription before commitments."
    }
  ],
